# Technical requirements (hackathon)

These six rows are **product requirements**. Identify / Generate / Defend already have Streamlit views. **Closed Loop, Real-time, and Novelty are backend/API capabilities — do not add new UI pages for them** unless the user asks.

| Requirement | Meaning | Implementation | Metric |
|---|---|---|---|
| Identify | Attack discovery engine | Agentic research + threat-intel ingest | Distinct attack families |
| Generate | Synthetic attack generator | LLM briefing + family overlay simulator + CTGAN/TVAE (bootstrap fallback) | Fidelity (KS/WD) + attack success rate |
| Defend | Fraud classifier | XGBoost/LightGBM (HistGB fallback) + optional relational/GNN head | Precision, Recall, F1, AUC, FPR |
| Closed Loop | Adversarial feedback | Red generate → blue score → failure analysis → retrain | Attack success before vs after |
| Real-time | Streaming detection | FastAPI `/detect` batch inference; Kafka optional, skip for demo | Latency &lt;100ms demo, &lt;50ms production narrative |
| Novelty | Emerging attacks | Threat intel + research agent + adversarial optimizer | Coverage of attacks not in training data |

## Build rules

- Incremental: about five changes per batch. Do not rebuild the research dump.
- Defensive only: hypotheses and overlays, no phishing copy, exploits, or live payment-rail attacks.
- Closed Loop lives in `backend/closed_loop.py`, `AdversarialOptimizer`, `FeedbackAgent`, `POST /evaluate/loop`. Robustness = holdout attack success before vs after retrain.
- Real-time = FastAPI batch `/detect` with measured latency. Do not add Kafka unless asked.
- Novelty = hold-out / washed / adversarial rows the initial detector did not train on. Report novel coverage, do not fake unseen families if they are already in `TRAIN_FAMILY_WEIGHTS`.
- Streamlit is the demo shell for Identify / Generate / Defend (and the existing loop viewer). New work on Closed Loop / Real-time / Novelty should land in backend + API first.
